nitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkcA2AÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;J0TNJK7QbdbDWzxpze6R0xWM85X-tQ6cj1QHONfaiQUÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkc1.0ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AzJY_oW-n6_g_c05grx__XaX7s64XuJJQwyHUTPRAOwÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkyëAt a July 2026 photocall in London, actor Zendaya appeared wearing a pair of gold earrings fashioned from 3,000-year-old archaeological discs [Zendaya‚Äôs Earrings Are Part of a Much Bigger Problem](https://hyperallergic.com/zendayas-earrings-are-part-of-a-much-bigger-problem/). The jewelry, which has become a focal point of public scrutiny, was acquired and mounted by a jeweler who set the ancient components into 18-karat gold with diamonds. These artifacts have reportedly been linked to the Ziwiye hoard, a treasure reputedly discovered by villagers in northwestern Iran in 1947.

## A Market in Ancient Fragments

The commodification of such antiquities relies on a process that effectively detaches objects from their historical and cultural context [Zendaya‚Äôs Earrings Are Part of a Much Bigger Problem](https://hyperallergic.com/zendayas-earrings-are-part-of-a-much-bigger-problem/). While the discs were repurposed for contemporary luxury wear, scholars and critics note that their presence in the private market‚Äîand eventually on the red carpet‚Äîobscures the underlying reality of their origin. Many such objects circulating in current collections lack documented provenance, leaving their journey from excavation sites to jewelry houses untraceable and their original funerary or ritual function ignored.

## The Costs of Aesthetic Consumption

The display of these earrings has prompted immediate backlash from archaeologists and cultural commentators who argue that the performative use of ancient history constitutes a form of exoticism [Zendaya‚Äôs Earrings Are Part of a Much Bigger Problem](https://hyperallergic.com/zendayas-earrings-are-part-of-a-much-bigger-problem/). Critics have pointed to the timing of this trend, noting that it unfolds amid ongoing reports of cultural destruction and conflict in the region where such artifacts originated. By treating these fragments as decorative, the fashion industry participates in a market that rarely accounts for the physical or ethical cost of looting or the illicit dismantling of archaeological sites.

## Epistemic Loss and Permanent Alteration

Unlike restoration efforts that seek to stabilize an object for research, the repurposing of historical artifacts often involves irreversible physical changes, such as drilling or cutting [Zendaya‚Äôs Earrings Are Part of a Much Bigger Problem](https://hyperallergic.com/zendayas-earrings-are-part-of-a-much-bigger-problem/). This transformation into contemporary jewelry effectively silences the information the object might have yielded regarding its provenance or historical use. The practice remains common, with various ancient components being restrung into necklaces or bracelets, regardless of their cultural origin. Ultimately, this trend highlights a tension between the global market‚Äôs appetite for luxury goods and the preservation of finite archaeological records that are systematically undone by the demand for status.ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;57OVW5gaKitl7rNw6dR0WjPVcZFTweZyJoGq8O7L4u8ÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx9ni:///sha-256;tv4OpKnS_uQP4XAkWG_8HO3ZI73164nwRg-6Sl_5GGsÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;3XjMyDWpykdVSjy8YTWBIMu0eiSY6rc5FkrCaQXFAf0ÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx9ni:///sha-256;h51ldc1l7JdXbYfZYaPOBzZg89uGBezGLucdRHHsUboÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;IfKsj54E_BdPHi_mz9b7W5hcGl2nroO-wYYfD_9TkpYÉdpairÉdleftÅdstarÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÉcsumÅdunitÅdunitÇdmark`ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DPDAvfo0NZS_9dxIY01ftEmLLcIlJMVRT5sN0s-cncQÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx%https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreamsÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;iQk3nq2MdD-TZKtlhr-E2WujuemORvb_JFqbnhECTH4ÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx%urn:ame:newswire-editorial-production