Unlike restoration efforts that seek to stabilize an object for research, the repurposing of historical artifacts often involves irreversible physical changes, such as drilling or cutting [Zendaya‚Äôs Earrings Are Part of a Much Bigger Problem](https://hyperallergic.com/zendayas-earrings-are-part-of-a-much-bigger-problem/). This transformation into contemporary jewelry effectively silences the information the object might have yielded regarding its provenance or historical use. The practice remains common, with various ancient components being restrung into necklaces or bracelets, regardless of their cultural origin. Ultimately, this trend highlights a tension between the global market‚Äôs appetite for luxury goods and the preservation of finite archaeological records that are systematically undone by the demand for status.ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;J8I_jE8VbiL7FwTGt2AA1Z994TcO7mldD0wJyzYi5skÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkxRmnProseContributionSettlementÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Hym4DH-Jk5S5Ubt9-2LxxHDK8NqUJ1CQaUGdbj9CSCIÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx9ni:///sha-256;h51ldc1l7JdXbYfZYaPOBzZg89uGBezGLucdRHHsUboÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4SGapV7CfEyM3TogL9J-mCv7yyn2fOod6DBL9014zsMÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx$https://koios.news/activitypub/actorÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;IHB7nE19RsdXRUonaLNqhpeWNyXFYqmA5czk9XS-zUYÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkfAcceptÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;4yBOyI9uPBTb3V2_g95VUvrOHRNazMSPFpw2wX9kGMAÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx2026-07-21T15:14:25.009ZÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasef